content.text:
I found one root cause: the `attractions` service went down and stayed down for the rest of the incident window. Its effect reached users through `frontend`, which returns HTTP 500 on three attraction-related paths. The small `reservation` shift is not a second fault: its median is unchanged, it produces no errors, and `frontend` latency on its calls is not meaningfully affected.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "attractions",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, time, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.deployment.available' AND attr_k8s_deployment_name='attractions' ORDER BY time",
          "claim": "attractions deployment available count is 0 from 09:30:35 through the end of the abnormal window, desired stays 1."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name, max(time) last_seen FROM normal_metrics_sum WHERE metric='k8s.pod.uptime' AND service_name='attractions' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "The attractions pod attractions-7c66cb7c79-dz25m emits uptime only in the normal period, last seen 09:29:15."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name LIKE 'attractions.Attractions/%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "In the abnormal period attractions emits no server spans; all frontend client calls to it end in Error within about 0.02 ms."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "attractions",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /cinema','HTTP /museums','HTTP /restaurants') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "frontend's HTTP /cinema, /museums and /restaurants return 500 Error in abnormal period (about 492 requests), while normal period returns 200."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

